{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n \\\"StreamableHttp|StreamableHTTP|streamableHttp|text/event-stream|EventStream|shared\\\" packages/server -g '\"'!dist'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"packages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.examples.ts:2: * Type-checked examples for `streamableHttp.ts`.\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.examples.ts:11:import { WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport } from './streamableHttp';\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.examples.ts:16:async function WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport_stateful() {\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.examples.ts:17:    //#region WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport_stateful\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.examples.ts:20:    const transport = new WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport({\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.examples.ts:25:    //#endregion WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport_stateful\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.examples.ts:31:async function WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport_stateless() {\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.examples.ts:32:    //#region WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport_stateless\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.examples.ts:33:    const transport = new WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport({\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.examples.ts:36:    //#endregion WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport_stateless\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.examples.ts:46:function WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport_hono(transport: WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport) {\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.examples.ts:47:    //#region WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport_hono\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.examples.ts:51:    //#endregion WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport_hono\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.examples.ts:57:function WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport_workers(transport: WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport) {\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.examples.ts:58:    //#region WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport_workers\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.examples.ts:64:    //#endregion WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport_workers\npackages/server/src/shimsWorkerd.ts:22:    throw new Error('StdioServerTransport is not supported in this environment. Use StreamableHTTPServerTransport instead.');\npackages/server/src/shimsBrowser.ts:17:    throw new Error('StdioServerTransport is not supported in this environment. Use StreamableHTTPServerTransport instead.');\npackages/server/src/server/listenRouter.ts:253:                'Content-Type': 'text/event-stream',\npackages/server/CHANGELOG.md:9:    The codemod now rewrites `Protocol` and `mergeCapabilities` imports from `shared/protocol.js` to the client or server package root, like the module's other symbols, instead of dropping them with an action-required marker.\npackages/server/CHANGELOG.md:30:- [#2477](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2477) [`8e1d2e9`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/8e1d2e92b1720d2520122b3a5f20ea084edaf3c4) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - Move the schema source modules (spec schemas, OAuth schemas, protocol constants) into `@modelcontextprotocol/core` and resolve them from there as a regular runtime dependency instead of bundling a private copy into each package. An application importing more than one of the packages now evaluates a single shared schema graph with shared object identity. `@modelcontextprotocol/core` gains a `./internal` subpath (SDK-internal contract; may change in any release) and the four packages now version together.\npackages/server/CHANGELOG.md:264:    **2025-era delivery-channel change (spec-conformance correction).** On a 2025-era sessionful Streamable HTTP transport, handler-emitted log messages now ride the per-request POST response stream instead of the standalone GET stream. This is a correction to the 2025-11-25 specification: `docs/specification/2025-11-25/basic/transports.mdx` §\"Sending Messages to the Server\" item 6 says JSON-RPC messages on the POST response stream SHOULD relate to the originating client request, and §\"Listening for Messages from the Server\" item 4 says messages on the GET stream SHOULD be unrelated to any concurrently-running client request — so a log emitted from a handler context belongs on the POST stream. Clients reading handler logs off the standalone GET stream will now see them on the per-request POST stream instead. The eventStore-resumable case (a log emitted after `closeSSE()` while the client has not yet reconnected) is handled by the store-first persistence behavior in `WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport.send()`. The session-scoped `Server.sendLoggingMessage()` API is unchanged.\npackages/server/CHANGELOG.md:266:- [#2286](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2286) [`1823aae`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/1823aae891837ebb5e3db885ec635f9efefd5771) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - `WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport`: request-related events (progress, `ctx.mcpReq.notify`, handler-emitted log) and the final response are now persisted to the configured `eventStore` whenever the request is in flight, regardless of whether a live SSE writer currently exists — mirroring the standalone-SSE path's store-first semantics. This fixes the `closeSSE()` poll-and-replay drop (events emitted after `closeSSE()` were previously silently lost) and aligns with the 2025-11-25 specification (\"disconnection SHOULD NOT be interpreted as the client cancelling its request\"). When an `eventStore` is configured, a final response sent while no per-request stream is connected is stored for replay and returns cleanly instead of throwing \"No connection established\"; a `Last-Event-ID` reconnect after the request has been retired replays the stored response and then closes the resumed stream. When no `eventStore` is configured, the same condition is surfaced via `onerror` (the response is undeliverable) and the request id is retired.\npackages/server/CHANGELOG.md:339:  StreamableHTTPServerTransport.close() with re-entrant guard\npackages/server/CHANGELOG.md:342:  optional callback and function properties on `WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransportOptions` (`sessionIdGenerator`, `onsessioninitialized`, `onsessionclosed`) and corresponding private fields.\npackages/server/CHANGELOG.md:479:  silently swallowed by adding missing `onerror` callback invocations before all `createJsonErrorResponse` calls in `WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport`. This ensures errors like parse failures, invalid headers, and session validation errors are properly reported via the\npackages/server/src/server/perRequestTransport.ts:390:                    'Content-Type': 'text/event-stream',\npackages/server/src/server/createMcpHandler.ts:69:import { WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport } from './streamableHttp';\npackages/server/src/server/createMcpHandler.ts:186:     * pub/sub backend; the same instance can be shared across handlers.\npackages/server/src/server/createMcpHandler.ts:320:            const transport = new WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport({ sessionIdGenerator: undefined });\npackages/server/src/server/createMcpHandler.ts:335:            if (response.body === null || mediaTypeEssence(response.headers.get('content-type')) !== 'text/event-stream') {\npackages/server/src/server/createMcpHandler.ts:394: * The entry's classification step (shared with isLegacyRequest)\npackages/server/src/server/createMcpHandler.ts:505: *             // e.g. an existing sessionful WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport wiring\npackages/server/src/index.ts:71:    WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransportOptions\npackages/server/src/index.ts:72:} from './server/streamableHttp';\npackages/server/src/index.ts:73:export { WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport } from './server/streamableHttp';\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.ts:7: * For Node.js Express/HTTP compatibility, use {@linkcode @modelcontextprotocol/node!NodeStreamableHTTPServerTransport | NodeStreamableHTTPServerTransport} which wraps this transport.\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.ts:78: * Configuration options for {@linkcode WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport}\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.ts:80:export interface WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransportOptions {\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.ts:104:     * {@linkcode WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport} after a request is completed while still keeping the\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.ts:198: * ```ts source=\"./streamableHttp.examples.ts#WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport_stateful\"\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.ts:201: * const transport = new WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport({\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.ts:209: * ```ts source=\"./streamableHttp.examples.ts#WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport_stateless\"\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.ts:210: * const transport = new WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport({\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.ts:216: * ```ts source=\"./streamableHttp.examples.ts#WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport_hono\"\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.ts:223: * ```ts source=\"./streamableHttp.examples.ts#WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport_workers\"\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.ts:231:export class WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransport implements Transport {\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.ts:256:    constructor(options: WebStandardStreamableHTTPServerTransportOptions = {}) {\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.ts:429:        // The client MUST include an Accept header, listing text/event-stream as a supported content type.\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.ts:431:        if (!acceptHeader?.includes('text/event-stream')) {\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.ts:432:            this.onerror?.(new Error('Not Acceptable: Client must accept text/event-stream'));\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.ts:433:            return this.createJsonErrorResponse(406, -32_000, 'Not Acceptable: Client must accept text/event-stream');\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.ts:482:            'Content-Type': 'text/event-stream',\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.ts:538:                'Content-Type': 'text/event-stream',\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.ts:683:            // The client MUST include an Accept header, listing both application/json and text/event-stream as supported content types.\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.ts:686:            if (!acceptHeader?.includes('application/json') || !acceptHeader.includes('text/event-stream')) {\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.ts:687:                this.onerror?.(new Error('Not Acceptable: Client must accept both application/json and text/event-stream'));\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.ts:691:                    'Not Acceptable: Client must accept both application/json and text/event-stream'\npackages/server/src/server/streamableHttp.ts:839:                'Content-Type': 'text/event-stream',\npackages/server/src/server/middleware/oauthMetadata.ts:120:                // without this a shared cache would replay one preflight's\npackages/server/src/server/server.ts:278:                // list is a shared module constant.\npackages/server/test/server/createMcpHandler.test.ts:64:            Accept: 'application/json, text/event-stream',\npackages/server/test/server/createMcpHandler.test.ts:752:        expect(response.headers.get('content-type')).toContain('text/event-stream');\npackages/server/test/server/createMcpHandler.test.ts:776